@startuml AgentPay Dispute Sequence
!theme plain
title Deterministic dispute classification

actor Claimant
actor Seller
participant "Go API" as API
participant "Dispute rules" as Rules
database "DynamoDB" as DDB
participant "Evidence verifier" as Evidence

Claimant -> API : POST /v1/disputes
API -> DDB : load transaction and existing dispute
API -> Evidence : load chain and verify hashes/signatures
Evidence --> API : valid/invalid + events
API -> Rules : reason + transaction + evidence facts

alt unauthorized claim disproved by payment authorization
  Rules --> API : denied
else duplicate, wrong amount, or failed delivery
  Rules --> API : refund_recommended
else quality/output claim
  Rules --> API : seller_review
else invalid evidence chain
  Rules --> API : seller_review + integrity alert
end

API -> DDB : persist result idempotently
API --> Claimant : 201 dispute with explanation

opt status = refund_recommended and payment is finalized
  Seller -> API : POST refund-records\nIdempotency-Key + exact refund metadata
  API -> API : authenticate owner + validate\namount/asset/network/finality/state
  API -> DDB : append one ManualRefundRecord
  API --> Seller : 201 record\nexact replay returns same response
end
@enduml
